## Key Analytical Observations

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Q3FY25 loss quarter drags 9M PAT sharply lower.</b> Cumulative 9MFY25 PAT of <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">₹10.83 cr</span> is down materially versus the run-rate implied by 1HFY25 (~₹16.68 cr as at 30 Sep 2024). This indicates Q3FY25 standalone was a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">loss-making quarter</span> (approx. ₹(50.87) cr per NL-2 quarterly column), consistent with the Reserves & Surplus roll-forward in the balance sheet schedule (opening balance ~₹489.05 cr vs. period-end balance of profit ~₹479.74 cr).
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Combined ratio above 100%.</b> The 9MFY25 combined ratio of <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">105%</span> (claims ratio <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">67%</span> + expense ratio <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">38%</span>) signals the core underwriting book remained loss-making before investment income, which is the primary driver of the weak bottom-line performance noted above.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Solvency comfortably above regulatory minimum.</b> The reported solvency ratio of <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">1.56x</span> remains above the IRDAI-mandated 1.50x threshold, indicating adequate capital buffer despite the weak underwriting profitability during the period.
</div>

### Data Gaps
- **Retail health GWP** and **Retail health market share**: Not disclosed in the statutory NL-4/NL-35/NL-36 schedules, which split premium only by line of business (Health/PA/Travel) and acquisition channel — not by Retail vs. Group segment. No separate 9MFY25 investor presentation (which typically carries this cut) was located among the fetched sources.
- **IFRS-basis PAT, Claims ratio**: Care Health Insurance Ltd is an Indian IRDAI-regulated non-life insurer that reports exclusively under Indian GAAP/IRDAI regulatory norms; no IFRS-basis figures exist in the statutory filings reviewed.
- The **Q4 FY24-25 disclosure** (covering the period ended 31 March 2025) was excluded as it falls outside the 9MFY25 (Apr–Dec 2024) scope of this request.</ans>
